1
00:00:03,453 --> 00:00:05,333
Hey, what's your name again?

2
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:07,167
It's Mungkorn.

3
00:00:07,192 --> 00:00:08,355
- Mungkorn?
- Yes, sir.

4
00:00:08,379 --> 00:00:09,276
What are you singing?

5
00:00:14,276 --> 00:00:15,779
I'll go with 'Wai Jai Dai Gah.'

6
00:00:15,864 --> 00:00:16,993
Wai Jai Dai Gah?

7
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:19,356
- Yeah.
- Alright, then.

8
00:00:25,046 --> 00:00:29,236
♪Back in the day,
wherever we went wandering,♪

9
00:00:29,286 --> 00:00:35,139
♪We were always together,
laughing at everything♪

10
00:00:35,651 --> 00:00:40,194
♪But then you met that city girl,♪

11
00:00:40,218 --> 00:00:44,916
♪That's when you'd do anything
just to please her♪

12
00:00:45,559 --> 00:00:50,173
♪Can those red lips really be trusted?♪

13
00:00:50,359 --> 00:00:54,973
♪Can that pretty face
really be trusted?♪

14
00:00:55,316 --> 00:00:59,796
♪Coming from so far away,
can she be trusted?♪

15
00:00:59,852 --> 00:01:05,393
♪She's not me,
can she really be trusted?♪

16
00:01:11,303 --> 00:01:12,841
You were great, Mungkorn.

17
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:13,756
Thanks.

18
00:01:16,213 --> 00:01:17,791
And what about that guy?

19
00:01:18,475 --> 00:01:19,780
You're not returning
to your table, are you?

20
00:01:20,326 --> 00:01:21,501
Can we have a toast before I go?

21
00:01:21,525 --> 00:01:23,436
- Sure.
- My boy wants me. I've gotta go.

22
00:01:23,673 --> 00:01:24,532
Okay.

23
00:01:25,399 --> 00:01:26,339
See you around.

24
00:01:34,779 --> 00:01:38,126
I had no idea
you had such a great voice, Mungkorn.

25
00:01:39,796 --> 00:01:40,579
Hey.

26
00:01:41,459 --> 00:01:42,846
You called me back here...

27
00:01:43,766 --> 00:01:45,305
cause you wanted me
to flirt with you instead, right?

28
00:01:46,486 --> 00:01:49,741
I just wanted to remind you
what we're actually here for today.

29
00:01:49,979 --> 00:01:52,839
Thear, if you keep buying drinks
for every girl here,

30
00:01:53,099 --> 00:01:54,252
you're gonna get wasted for real.

31
00:01:54,731 --> 00:01:57,239
I'm not that drunk. I'm good.

32
00:01:58,644 --> 00:01:59,399
I knew it.

33
00:01:59,804 --> 00:02:00,906
I'm fine. I'm good.

34
00:02:00,964 --> 00:02:04,083
Anyway, where's the bathroom?
Better safe than sorry.

35
00:02:04,110 --> 00:02:05,212
I'll take you.

36
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:07,405
Hey, you're acting like I'm wasted.
I'm fine.

37
00:02:07,477 --> 00:02:09,017
If you're not,
then what's gotten into you?

38
00:02:10,284 --> 00:02:12,436
- You guys wait here.
- I'm good.

39
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:18,457
Whoa, hold on a sec.

40
00:02:27,651 --> 00:02:28,753
Are you okay?

41
00:02:28,778 --> 00:02:32,219
- Ins...
- S... Sweetheart?

42
00:02:32,671 --> 00:02:34,726
Wow, you're really calling me that?

43
00:02:35,831 --> 00:02:37,556
I'm kinda getting a good buzz.

44
00:02:38,919 --> 00:02:39,767
Should we go for it?

45
00:02:39,866 --> 00:02:40,854
Right here?

46
00:02:45,066 --> 00:02:46,239
If you say so.

47
00:02:47,259 --> 00:02:49,556
I'm getting pretty tipsy, too.

48
00:02:52,573 --> 00:02:53,139
Hey...

49
00:02:55,046 --> 00:02:56,066
I'm getting the chills.

50
00:02:57,453 --> 00:02:58,439
I'm feeling it now.

51
00:03:01,013 --> 00:03:01,886
How do you feel?

52
00:03:01,911 --> 00:03:03,032
You've got a nice ass.

53
00:03:06,259 --> 00:03:07,012
Are they all gone yet?

54
00:03:07,566 --> 00:03:08,559
- Not yet.
- Keep going.

55
00:03:11,259 --> 00:03:11,926
Are they gone now?

56
00:03:13,905 --> 00:03:14,772
They're all gone.

57
00:03:16,978 --> 00:03:17,592
Look,

58
00:03:17,892 --> 00:03:19,601
we don't know
who's working with them.

59
00:03:19,859 --> 00:03:21,956
Whatever you're going to call me,
you'd better be careful.

60
00:03:22,026 --> 00:03:22,916
Yes, Inspector.

61
00:03:24,606 --> 00:03:25,264
My bad.

62
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:26,759
Has the informant sent the intel yet?

63
00:03:26,904 --> 00:03:28,764
Yes. His name is Ronnaphop.

64
00:03:28,964 --> 00:03:30,732
He's suspected to be
the leader of the Black Bull gang,

65
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:32,750
the major drug dealer in this area.

66
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:35,349
Informant says he should be
getting to this club around midnight.

67
00:03:35,417 --> 00:03:36,704
He's the real deal, huh?

68
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:40,009
I'd say he's almost
as good-looking as me.

69
00:03:41,349 --> 00:03:42,984
This is the photo from his social media.

70
00:03:43,145 --> 00:03:44,279
This is him.

71
00:03:44,523 --> 00:03:47,196
Damn, he edited it so much
he looks like a different person.

72
00:03:48,732 --> 00:03:50,436
(The Black Bull has entered the cave.)

73
00:03:53,396 --> 00:03:54,154
Let's go.

74
00:03:54,858 --> 00:03:57,600
- Wait, Inspector.
- Hey, stop calling me that.

75
00:03:57,672 --> 00:03:58,658
Your fly is open.

76
00:04:04,664 --> 00:04:06,199
Just when I'm in a rush. Seriously?

77
00:04:06,248 --> 00:04:07,264
We're running out of time.

78
00:04:07,552 --> 00:04:09,196
It's just... stuck.

79
00:04:09,866 --> 00:04:10,801
It won't budge.

80
00:04:13,312 --> 00:04:14,465
Please allow me to help you.

81
00:04:15,052 --> 00:04:15,836
Help how?

82
00:04:17,199 --> 00:04:17,947
Stay still.

83
00:04:18,145 --> 00:04:19,194
I'll give the signal.

84
00:04:19,865 --> 00:04:22,426
Three, two, one.

85
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:24,986
All set.

86
00:04:28,352 --> 00:04:29,824
Yeah, thanks a lot.

87
00:04:29,986 --> 00:04:30,624
Let's move.

88
00:04:30,966 --> 00:04:31,636
Go.

89
00:04:48,332 --> 00:04:49,926
Shall we start the operation now?

90
00:04:51,886 --> 00:04:52,544
No.

91
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,236
This is my specialty.
Leave it to me.

92
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:07,566
Oh...

93
00:05:08,086 --> 00:05:09,146
Hi, boss.

94
00:05:09,632 --> 00:05:11,156
Mind if I join you for a dance?

95
00:05:11,565 --> 00:05:12,446
Not at all.

96
00:05:12,879 --> 00:05:14,746
Fair skin's always been my weakness.

97
00:05:14,771 --> 00:05:16,826
Aw, you're such a smooth talker.

98
00:05:20,826 --> 00:05:23,516
Wow, your hands are so soft.

99
00:05:39,926 --> 00:05:41,753
Easy there, boss.

100
00:05:50,682 --> 00:05:51,716
Wait, you're a cop?

101
00:05:52,589 --> 00:05:53,096
Freeze!

102
00:06:00,039 --> 00:06:00,672
Stop!

103
00:06:01,006 --> 00:06:01,686
Get on your knees!

104
00:06:01,992 --> 00:06:05,626
You're under arrest for drug trafficking
and organized crime.

105
00:06:05,679 --> 00:06:06,954
- Get down!
- You have the right to remain silent.

106
00:06:06,976 --> 00:06:07,766
- Stay down!
- Anything you say

107
00:06:07,776 --> 00:06:08,923
can and will be used
against you in a court of law.

108
00:06:09,379 --> 00:06:10,824
Oh, but if you do talk,

109
00:06:11,012 --> 00:06:12,773
you're getting busted anyway, boss.

110
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:15,594
- You've got no proof.
- Keep your mouth shut.

111
00:06:16,066 --> 00:06:16,672
Sarge!

112
00:06:25,712 --> 00:06:26,516
How was that?

113
00:06:27,253 --> 00:06:30,320
(Inspector Thear:
The cunning and irresistible inspector)

114
00:06:30,676 --> 00:06:32,793
All suspects are in custody
along with the evidence.

115
00:06:38,859 --> 00:06:39,567
Hey, hey!

116
00:06:39,799 --> 00:06:41,392
- Stay still!
- What is wrong with you?

117
00:06:41,946 --> 00:06:42,516
Hey!

118
00:06:43,192 --> 00:06:44,340
- Inspector!
- Sarge, get out of there.

119
00:06:44,364 --> 00:06:45,285
He might be faking it.

120
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:47,276
I don't think he is.
His lips are turning blue.

121
00:06:47,372 --> 00:06:49,116
Listen to me. Get away from him.

122
00:06:49,156 --> 00:06:50,686
We should save him first,
or it'll be too late.

123
00:06:50,711 --> 00:06:51,996
- Hey!
- Excuse me, Inspector.

124
00:06:59,632 --> 00:07:00,272
Inspector!

125
00:07:00,759 --> 00:07:01,639
Please call an ambulance.

126
00:07:01,664 --> 00:07:02,426
I am.

127
00:07:03,952 --> 00:07:04,594
Hey, stay still.

128
00:07:04,866 --> 00:07:06,313
- Freeze!
- Drop the gun.

129
00:07:07,006 --> 00:07:08,559
- Drop it.
- I told you to drop the damn gun!

130
00:07:08,899 --> 00:07:09,746
Drop it!

131
00:07:09,986 --> 00:07:10,899
Okay, okay.

132
00:07:10,926 --> 00:07:11,932
Put it on...

133
00:07:13,679 --> 00:07:14,156
Ugh!

134
00:07:30,373 --> 00:07:33,473
(Sergeant Mungkorn:
Kind but not easy to break)

135
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:39,993
(Inspector Phuwin: Fierce, tough,
and intense. The pride of Mae Sai.)

136
00:07:43,646 --> 00:07:46,479
(Sergeant Lukplub: The youngest
but not the weakest, Phuwin's babe)

137
00:07:58,113 --> 00:07:59,600
Inspector, he's getting away!

138
00:08:03,259 --> 00:08:03,872
Hey!

139
00:08:09,873 --> 00:08:10,872
Goddammit!

140
00:08:13,966 --> 00:08:14,666
Sh*t!

141
00:08:19,432 --> 00:08:19,996
F*ck...

142
00:09:11,993 --> 00:09:12,993
Go. Get up there.

143
00:09:14,859 --> 00:09:15,519
Come on.

144
00:09:16,325 --> 00:09:16,912
Go up there.

145
00:09:16,999 --> 00:09:18,379
- I'll leave this to you, Lieutenant.
- Yes, sir.

146
00:09:20,819 --> 00:09:22,072
Good luck, boss.

147
00:09:29,493 --> 00:09:30,834
Thanks a lot, Mungkorn.

148
00:09:31,492 --> 00:09:33,207
If you hadn't backed me up,

149
00:09:33,518 --> 00:09:34,558
I would've been in deep trouble.

150
00:09:34,638 --> 00:09:37,344
I should be apologizing to you
for disobeying your orders.

151
00:09:38,185 --> 00:09:39,585
The whole plan almost fell apart.

152
00:09:40,945 --> 00:09:41,744
You get it now?

153
00:09:43,032 --> 00:09:45,596
Don't be so stubborn next time.
You need to listen to me.

154
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:52,726
It was pretty fun, though.

155
00:09:54,905 --> 00:09:57,424
We don't get to work together often.
It reminds me of the old days.

156
00:09:59,199 --> 00:10:02,072
Did Phuwin and Lukplub already leave?

157
00:10:02,097 --> 00:10:03,860
Oh, they already did.

158
00:10:04,265 --> 00:10:05,300
They left together.

159
00:10:05,399 --> 00:10:07,836
Man, what is it with couples?

160
00:10:07,966 --> 00:10:09,672
Don't they get sick of each other?

161
00:10:09,759 --> 00:10:10,879
Aren't they too clingy?

162
00:10:11,179 --> 00:10:13,156
As if you don't want a partner yourself.

163
00:10:14,025 --> 00:10:15,740
Well, I really don't.

164
00:10:16,092 --> 00:10:18,692
Come on, I value my freedom.

165
00:10:18,865 --> 00:10:20,787
Having to worry about someone?
No, thanks.

166
00:10:20,812 --> 00:10:22,505
I'd rather stay single.
It's way easier.

167
00:10:24,016 --> 00:10:27,436
All those words, and what you mean
is that you're a flirt, huh?

168
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:30,716
Wait, maybe you just
haven't found the one.

169
00:10:39,359 --> 00:10:40,304
And what about you?

170
00:10:41,106 --> 00:10:42,113
Have you found them?

171
00:10:42,756 --> 00:10:43,606
Have you found the one?

172
00:10:59,439 --> 00:11:00,716
Watch out! A gun!

173
00:11:12,553 --> 00:11:13,287
Inspector!

174
00:11:13,612 --> 00:11:15,156
Inspector, hang in there.

175
00:11:16,406 --> 00:11:17,384
Help!

176
00:11:18,846 --> 00:11:19,612
Help!

177
00:11:21,599 --> 00:11:22,241
Inspector!

178
00:11:22,452 --> 00:11:23,464
Inspector Thear!

179
00:11:24,146 --> 00:11:27,196
Inspector Thear!

180
00:11:34,623 --> 00:11:37,603
(Yin as Theartha)

181
00:11:42,543 --> 00:11:45,270
(War as Mungkorn)

182
00:11:49,412 --> 00:11:51,760
(Shane as Phuwin)

183
00:11:52,199 --> 00:11:55,239
(Boss as Lukplub)

184
00:11:57,619 --> 00:11:59,346
(Kit as Kanin)

185
00:11:59,605 --> 00:12:01,559
(Tang as Nadol)

186
00:12:05,036 --> 00:12:10,279
(Tae as Saming)

187
00:12:41,316 --> 00:12:42,774
Your blood pressure is normal.

188
00:12:42,922 --> 00:12:44,066
My blood pressure might be fine,

189
00:12:44,329 --> 00:12:45,703
but my heart rate certainly isn't.

190
00:12:46,475 --> 00:12:47,748
So, do you have a boyfriend?

191
00:12:50,915 --> 00:12:51,828
Oh, Sarge.

192
00:12:51,995 --> 00:12:53,330
Man, you're such a buzzkill.

193
00:12:53,346 --> 00:12:54,735
I was just about to get an answer

194
00:12:54,742 --> 00:12:56,726
on whether the nurse was single or not.

195
00:12:57,581 --> 00:13:00,112
Your visitor is here,
so I'll take my leave now.

196
00:13:01,316 --> 00:13:02,694
That's two smiles in the bag.

197
00:13:04,022 --> 00:13:05,136
She might be taken.

198
00:13:05,389 --> 00:13:07,494
Your shoulder's been shot,

199
00:13:08,262 --> 00:13:10,266
yet you still have the energy
to flirt with the nurse?

200
00:13:10,736 --> 00:13:13,116
I don't flirt with my shoulder.
I use my mouth.

201
00:13:13,356 --> 00:13:15,386
And I'm kind of famous
for what I can do with it.

202
00:13:17,803 --> 00:13:21,051
Anyway, thanks for looking after me

203
00:13:21,196 --> 00:13:22,903
even though you didn't have to.

204
00:13:23,389 --> 00:13:26,397
I'm just doing my duty
as your subordinate.

205
00:13:26,695 --> 00:13:27,943
Doing your duty, huh?

206
00:13:29,055 --> 00:13:32,371
But I'm not even your direct superior.

207
00:13:33,382 --> 00:13:35,414
I'll just take it as...

208
00:13:36,809 --> 00:13:37,956
you're doing it because you care.

209
00:13:39,586 --> 00:13:41,386
Where is he? Is he awake?

210
00:13:42,109 --> 00:13:43,257
Thear, my boy.

211
00:13:43,629 --> 00:13:45,026
Thear!

212
00:13:45,363 --> 00:13:47,204
- My baby!
- Whoa, Mom. My shoulder!

213
00:13:47,228 --> 00:13:49,643
- My left shoulder.
- How are you? Are you okay?

214
00:13:49,668 --> 00:13:51,234
Hi, Mr. Thear...

215
00:13:53,921 --> 00:13:55,308
Where does it hurt?

216
00:13:55,554 --> 00:13:57,427
- My left shoulder, Mom.
- Where? Here?

217
00:13:57,452 --> 00:13:59,094
Yeah, around here. Don't touch it.

218
00:13:59,134 --> 00:14:00,254
But I'm fine.

219
00:14:00,414 --> 00:14:02,961
It's nowhere near my heart.
It's a piece of cake.

220
00:14:03,007 --> 00:14:04,249
Good afternoon, Lady Pharada.

221
00:14:04,747 --> 00:14:06,188
I'm Sergeant Mungkorn,

222
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,023
Inspector Thear's subordinate.

223
00:14:09,174 --> 00:14:10,334
I'm also...

224
00:14:10,767 --> 00:14:13,402
the reason he got shot.

225
00:14:14,573 --> 00:14:15,649
I am really sorry.

226
00:14:19,133 --> 00:14:21,613
Hey, Sarge. Don't be so dramatic.

227
00:14:21,638 --> 00:14:23,623
That thug was just shooting blindly.

228
00:14:23,648 --> 00:14:26,358
But I think you're seriously
out of luck this time.

229
00:14:27,767 --> 00:14:28,626
Or maybe...

230
00:14:28,933 --> 00:14:31,841
fate is really coming for you
just like the oracle said?

231
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:35,157
What fate are you talking about, Mom?
It's not that serious.

232
00:14:35,194 --> 00:14:36,556
Not that serious?

233
00:14:36,581 --> 00:14:39,096
This is basically "Final Destination."

234
00:14:40,989 --> 00:14:41,784
Cupid.

235
00:14:42,542 --> 00:14:43,349
On it.

236
00:14:44,983 --> 00:14:47,254
Damn, my car just broke down
out of nowhere.

237
00:14:47,876 --> 00:14:48,746
Whoa!

238
00:14:52,282 --> 00:14:54,826
Hey! You just hit a cop!

239
00:14:57,199 --> 00:14:58,914
You're delivering me food?

240
00:15:00,259 --> 00:15:02,459
It's you. You killed my dad!

241
00:15:02,976 --> 00:15:04,153
I didn't.

242
00:15:06,919 --> 00:15:08,132
I almost died.

243
00:15:19,442 --> 00:15:21,386
- There are more scenarios, too.
- Enough.

244
00:15:22,243 --> 00:15:23,984
I'm a police officer, Mom.

245
00:15:24,008 --> 00:15:26,986
Taking risks is just part of the job.

246
00:15:27,086 --> 00:15:30,807
But if that thug's aim
had been off by just a tiny bit...

247
00:15:30,816 --> 00:15:31,906
Stop it.

248
00:15:32,096 --> 00:15:32,858
And...

249
00:15:32,887 --> 00:15:35,236
if the bullet had hit your heart,

250
00:15:35,266 --> 00:15:37,746
you'd literally be gone.

251
00:15:43,996 --> 00:15:44,884
I don't care.

252
00:15:45,216 --> 00:15:47,444
I'm certain this incident
is a sign of your luck.

253
00:15:47,468 --> 00:15:48,816
As soon as you're discharged,

254
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,548
we're going to see the family oracle.

255
00:15:50,573 --> 00:15:52,194
- Cupid, book an appointment.
- Will do.

256
00:15:52,219 --> 00:15:54,176
That's nonsense, Mom.
I'm not going.

257
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,788
You know I don't believe in oracles.

258
00:15:55,812 --> 00:15:57,803
Every time we go,
she just talks a load of rubbish.

259
00:15:57,828 --> 00:15:59,128
She's just scamming us for money.

260
00:15:59,152 --> 00:16:01,613
- So, no booking yet?
- No! You have to go.

261
00:16:01,638 --> 00:16:04,199
No matter what,
your life is on the line here.

262
00:16:04,223 --> 00:16:06,231
It doesn't make sense.
It's a waste of time.

263
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:07,679
I'm doing this for your own sake.

264
00:16:07,703 --> 00:16:10,259
If it's for my sake,
you need to stop being so superstitious.

265
00:16:10,283 --> 00:16:11,378
Thear!

266
00:16:16,916 --> 00:16:18,476
You just don't understand
a mother's heart.

267
00:16:19,596 --> 00:16:20,786
Let's go, Cupid.

268
00:16:26,321 --> 00:16:28,777
Man, they're being
way too dramatic about this.

269
00:16:28,802 --> 00:16:30,217
It's not that big of a deal.

270
00:16:30,523 --> 00:16:32,617
If you didn't have anyone
caring about you,

271
00:16:33,016 --> 00:16:34,569
you'd really feel the difference.

272
00:16:35,062 --> 00:16:36,026
What's that supposed to mean?

273
00:16:36,842 --> 00:16:38,390
You're lucky, Inspector,

274
00:16:38,562 --> 00:16:41,466
to have a mother who cares so much
and tries to fix things for you.

275
00:16:41,614 --> 00:16:44,089
She's genuinely terrified of losing you.

276
00:16:44,322 --> 00:16:45,495
I think...

277
00:16:46,268 --> 00:16:48,454
even if you don't believe in oracles,

278
00:16:48,702 --> 00:16:51,742
taking just one day
to give her some peace of mind

279
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:53,915
shouldn't be too much
of a hassle, right?

280
00:16:54,162 --> 00:16:55,654
So, you're taking her side?

281
00:16:56,436 --> 00:16:58,426
Fine. I'll go.

282
00:16:59,446 --> 00:17:00,596
But you're coming with me.

283
00:17:01,436 --> 00:17:02,731
Wait, what do I have to do with this?

284
00:17:02,755 --> 00:17:04,746
Well, didn't you say you felt guilty?

285
00:17:05,009 --> 00:17:06,543
This is your chance to make it up to me.

286
00:17:14,396 --> 00:17:16,296
(Mother Tongnuan's Shrine)

287
00:17:21,056 --> 00:17:24,366
Gosh, this bad luck
won't give you a break, will it?

288
00:17:24,426 --> 00:17:26,506
I literally just
got out of the hospital.

289
00:17:26,626 --> 00:17:28,726
We could've at least waited
until the wound healed.

290
00:17:28,806 --> 00:17:29,446
Come on.

291
00:17:29,666 --> 00:17:32,516
Mother Tongnuan will keep you
safe and sound.

292
00:17:32,576 --> 00:17:33,896
She's incredibly accurate.

293
00:17:33,916 --> 00:17:35,956
Last time, she predicted
that I'd get a boyfriend.

294
00:17:36,376 --> 00:17:38,906
The very next day, I lost my virginity!

295
00:17:38,926 --> 00:17:41,146
That's just because
you were being such a flirt!

296
00:17:41,926 --> 00:17:44,926
Let's just get this over with
so we can go back to our lives

297
00:17:44,986 --> 00:17:46,346
and so you can stop
being so superstitious.

298
00:17:47,346 --> 00:17:48,806
Disrespectful the moment you arrive?

299
00:17:49,456 --> 00:17:52,286
Even if you don't believe,
you should show some respect, Inspector.

300
00:17:52,746 --> 00:17:56,126
Goodness, thank you
for scolding him for me.

301
00:17:56,946 --> 00:17:59,076
You're amazing.
How did you manage to bring my son here?

302
00:17:59,096 --> 00:18:01,346
Even though I'm his mother,
he wouldn't listen to me.

303
00:18:16,906 --> 00:18:17,906
We're here.

304
00:18:18,676 --> 00:18:20,546
I'll wait right here, then.

305
00:18:45,696 --> 00:18:47,356
You've finally arrived.

306
00:18:51,036 --> 00:18:52,606
This is my son.

307
00:18:53,076 --> 00:18:55,826
He's been having
a run of bad luck lately.

308
00:18:57,726 --> 00:18:59,706
I already know without you telling me.

309
00:19:00,416 --> 00:19:02,466
I can smell the stench of misfortune
from miles away.

310
00:19:04,106 --> 00:19:05,406
What do you see, Mother?

311
00:19:05,536 --> 00:19:07,706
What's going to happen to Mr. Thear?

312
00:19:07,726 --> 00:19:11,206
Your fate has been cursed since birth.

313
00:19:11,476 --> 00:19:13,846
Saturn is looming over your fate,

314
00:19:14,376 --> 00:19:16,416
and so is Uranus.

315
00:19:18,316 --> 00:19:19,836
What does that mean, Mother?

316
00:19:21,756 --> 00:19:23,286
It means...

317
00:19:25,036 --> 00:19:28,886
fate will take everything you own...

318
00:19:30,146 --> 00:19:32,566
even your life.

319
00:19:35,496 --> 00:19:36,286
And...

320
00:19:37,126 --> 00:19:41,306
is there any way to remedy this, Mother?

321
00:20:14,146 --> 00:20:20,166
You must find your soulmate
from your past life.

322
00:20:20,826 --> 00:20:26,526
Then you must marry that person
with heaven and earth as witnesses.

323
00:20:28,636 --> 00:20:29,846
Otherwise...

324
00:20:30,736 --> 00:20:33,786
it won't just be choking on a meatball

325
00:20:36,546 --> 00:20:38,266
or getting shot in the shoulder.

326
00:20:41,826 --> 00:20:46,256
But it will lead to your death
within six months.

327
00:20:46,876 --> 00:20:47,966
- Six months?
- Six months?

328
00:20:51,426 --> 00:20:52,376
I'm passing out.

329
00:20:53,643 --> 00:20:54,743
My Lady!

330
00:20:58,696 --> 00:21:00,666
Young man, would you like
to make merit for your birthday?

331
00:21:01,756 --> 00:21:02,616
Of course.

332
00:21:07,976 --> 00:21:13,346
You must marry someone born on Monday,
the 13th of October.

333
00:21:14,096 --> 00:21:16,866
Both their first and last names
must contain 'ro ruea'.

334
00:21:17,336 --> 00:21:18,336
Otherwise,

335
00:21:19,396 --> 00:21:22,236
this misfortune will follow you
until the day you die.

336
00:21:22,476 --> 00:21:24,786
So you mean he has to get married?

337
00:21:25,016 --> 00:21:25,576
Yes.

338
00:21:27,236 --> 00:21:30,016
You must hold a wedding ceremony

339
00:21:30,176 --> 00:21:32,626
and live together for six months.

340
00:21:34,336 --> 00:21:36,656
Then, your bad luck and karma
will finally be over.

341
00:21:37,556 --> 00:21:39,736
And you expect me
to just marry some stranger?

342
00:21:40,156 --> 00:21:42,186
Mom, are you crazy?
How is that supposed to help?

343
00:21:42,966 --> 00:21:45,126
If he doesn't believe it,
then let him be.

344
00:21:45,456 --> 00:21:47,576
He'll eventually come back to me.

345
00:21:48,316 --> 00:21:49,846
With a description that specific,

346
00:21:49,926 --> 00:21:51,236
where am I supposed to find them?

347
00:21:51,266 --> 00:21:52,716
Oh, should I ask the district chief?

348
00:21:52,746 --> 00:21:54,316
Have him pull up everyone's
birth records in the country?

349
00:21:56,876 --> 00:21:57,616
Fine.

350
00:21:57,886 --> 00:21:59,286
Well, if you're really that good,

351
00:21:59,316 --> 00:22:00,696
why don't you just hand them to me
on a silver platter?

352
00:22:00,746 --> 00:22:01,666
Bring that person to me,

353
00:22:01,686 --> 00:22:03,416
so I don't have to
waste my time looking.

354
00:22:03,626 --> 00:22:04,316
Serve them right up.

355
00:22:37,676 --> 00:22:39,056
(Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich,
born on Monday, October 13, 1997)

356
00:22:41,316 --> 00:22:44,346
(Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich,
born on Monday, October 13, 1997)

357
00:22:50,036 --> 00:22:52,576
Born on Monday, October 13th.

358
00:22:53,116 --> 00:22:55,046
Mr. Mungkorn...

359
00:22:55,176 --> 00:22:56,316
That consonant is in it.

360
00:22:57,756 --> 00:22:59,256
Phianwanich...

361
00:22:59,756 --> 00:23:01,556
There's another one in that, too!

362
00:23:03,866 --> 00:23:04,886
This is...

363
00:23:05,036 --> 00:23:06,096
That's mine.

364
00:23:13,636 --> 00:23:15,196
The wind is so strong.

365
00:23:16,776 --> 00:23:18,386
It blew this quite a long way.

366
00:23:19,826 --> 00:23:21,246
Wait, Mungkorn.

367
00:23:22,216 --> 00:23:23,806
Is something the matter?

368
00:23:24,346 --> 00:23:27,346
Thear, I've found your soulmate!

369
00:23:27,386 --> 00:23:30,706
A gift from heaven,
no district chief needed.

370
00:23:35,736 --> 00:23:38,496
You need to marry Mungkorn.

371
00:23:39,956 --> 00:23:40,626
- What?
- What?

372
00:23:58,646 --> 00:24:01,166
Mom, stop thinking about
that ridiculous marriage right now.

373
00:24:01,336 --> 00:24:03,386
It's only for six months.

374
00:24:03,406 --> 00:24:05,056
You can just get a divorce
once the six months are up.

375
00:24:05,086 --> 00:24:06,156
Only six months?

376
00:24:06,196 --> 00:24:08,616
I'm not going to waste my time
on some superstition of yours.

377
00:24:08,716 --> 00:24:10,506
If word gets out that I'm married,

378
00:24:10,526 --> 00:24:12,036
all the girls I've been seeing
will disappear.

379
00:24:12,086 --> 00:24:13,456
I've been on fire lately.

380
00:24:14,816 --> 00:24:16,266
Yeah, but it's hellfire
that's been following you around.

381
00:24:16,406 --> 00:24:17,756
There's no way, Mom.

382
00:24:17,786 --> 00:24:19,716
How can I marry someone I don't love?

383
00:24:19,736 --> 00:24:20,646
Just get married first,

384
00:24:20,666 --> 00:24:22,706
and you can work on
the relationship later.

385
00:24:22,726 --> 00:24:24,006
That sounds so old-fashioned.

386
00:24:24,006 --> 00:24:24,916
What century do you think we're in?

387
00:24:24,946 --> 00:24:26,476
It doesn't matter.

388
00:24:26,496 --> 00:24:28,116
Fate and fortune
have existed in every age.

389
00:24:28,146 --> 00:24:29,526
You don't have a choice.

390
00:24:29,556 --> 00:24:30,276
- I do!
- No, you don't.

391
00:24:30,296 --> 00:24:30,956
- I do!
- No.

392
00:24:30,976 --> 00:24:31,656
- I do!
- You don't!

393
00:24:31,681 --> 00:24:32,671
- What about me?
- You...

394
00:24:34,656 --> 00:24:36,366
Do I still have a choice?

395
00:24:38,286 --> 00:24:40,466
Even though I'm just a junior officer

396
00:24:40,656 --> 00:24:44,046
who's supposed to follow orders
and protect my superior,

397
00:24:44,526 --> 00:24:46,346
it's still my life, too.

398
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:50,556
I only want to
marry someone I truly love.

399
00:24:51,876 --> 00:24:53,506
Someone who'll stay by my side,

400
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:55,686
listen to me,

401
00:24:56,556 --> 00:24:58,006
share the good and bad with me,

402
00:24:58,846 --> 00:25:00,426
and spend our lives together.

403
00:25:02,296 --> 00:25:04,286
I don't want to marry Inspector Thear.

404
00:25:06,296 --> 00:25:07,606
Mungkorn...

405
00:25:08,076 --> 00:25:10,016
Honey, look...

406
00:25:10,216 --> 00:25:12,846
I really don't want to
force anyone into anything,

407
00:25:12,876 --> 00:25:15,296
but you understand a mother's concern,
don't you?

408
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:16,776
Yes.

409
00:25:17,136 --> 00:25:18,606
Could you please reconsider?

410
00:25:19,716 --> 00:25:22,226
Is there anything you want?
Just name it, and it's yours.

411
00:25:22,716 --> 00:25:25,176
The necklace from Titanic?
I'll go dive for it myself.

412
00:25:25,366 --> 00:25:26,506
That won't be necessary.

413
00:25:27,056 --> 00:25:27,766
It's just...

414
00:25:29,146 --> 00:25:30,666
I understand your feelings,
Lady Pharada.

415
00:25:31,846 --> 00:25:34,306
But marriage is a huge commitment.

416
00:25:34,506 --> 00:25:39,146
I think you should find someone else
to marry him.

417
00:25:39,256 --> 00:25:42,576
There must be plenty of other people
born at the exact same time

418
00:25:42,856 --> 00:25:44,006
as me.

419
00:25:44,016 --> 00:25:44,486
No, there aren't.

420
00:25:44,506 --> 00:25:45,476
- I'm sure there are.
- No.

421
00:25:46,006 --> 00:25:47,266
I'm really sorry.

422
00:25:47,826 --> 00:25:50,166
I have to head off to work
in Mae Sai now.

423
00:25:50,886 --> 00:25:52,026
Please excuse me, Lady Pharada.

424
00:25:52,916 --> 00:25:53,936
I'll be going now, Inspector.

425
00:26:03,326 --> 00:26:04,156
Can I leave now?

426
00:26:04,486 --> 00:26:05,326
To where?

427
00:26:06,566 --> 00:26:07,266
Oh...

428
00:26:07,946 --> 00:26:09,686
You can leave, Mr. Thear.

429
00:26:10,406 --> 00:26:11,866
But you'd better be careful

430
00:26:11,956 --> 00:26:15,956
because danger lurks
in every step you take.

431
00:26:25,076 --> 00:26:27,186
My Lady, what are we going to do now?

432
00:26:29,806 --> 00:26:31,496
You've underestimated me, Thear.

433
00:26:31,716 --> 00:26:34,356
There's no way I'm going to
let anything happen to my son.

434
00:26:34,886 --> 00:26:35,666
Just you wait and see.

435
00:26:39,156 --> 00:26:40,826
(Police Accommodation, Chiang Rai)

436
00:26:42,676 --> 00:26:43,846
Not tasty, Mungkorn?

437
00:26:44,136 --> 00:26:47,466
I ordered your favorite Northern laab
to welcome you back.

438
00:26:48,016 --> 00:26:49,166
It's tasty.

439
00:26:49,646 --> 00:26:51,276
It's just my stomach's
been a bit upset lately.

440
00:26:51,406 --> 00:26:52,726
Can't enjoy spicy food now.

441
00:26:53,596 --> 00:26:54,776
Phu's just like you.

442
00:26:55,296 --> 00:26:56,616
He has a sensitive stomach,
yet he won't stop.

443
00:26:56,816 --> 00:26:59,116
I always have to keep antacids
ready for him.

444
00:26:59,596 --> 00:27:00,626
He's so stubborn.

445
00:27:02,936 --> 00:27:04,446
And whose babe are you?

446
00:27:04,696 --> 00:27:06,906
I wonder who takes such good care of me.

447
00:27:09,216 --> 00:27:09,946
You guys are so cheesy.

448
00:27:10,476 --> 00:27:12,486
Hey, let me ask you something.

449
00:27:12,626 --> 00:27:14,786
Have you ever thought
about getting married?

450
00:27:15,816 --> 00:27:16,846
Of course we have.

451
00:27:17,186 --> 00:27:18,316
But we're in no rush, right?

452
00:27:18,962 --> 00:27:21,382
We're already happy
with the life we have together.

453
00:27:22,056 --> 00:27:22,786
What about you, Phu?

454
00:27:23,056 --> 00:27:24,126
I want to marry you, too.

455
00:27:24,856 --> 00:27:28,386
Why wouldn't I want to
marry my baby?

456
00:27:30,616 --> 00:27:33,456
Hypothetically, if you had to
marry someone you didn't love,

457
00:27:34,146 --> 00:27:34,956
would you still do it?

458
00:27:35,336 --> 00:27:36,896
Why are you asking that?

459
00:27:38,516 --> 00:27:39,416
Oh, no reason.

460
00:27:40,806 --> 00:27:45,206
I was just thinking about
when they had arranged marriages.

461
00:27:45,676 --> 00:27:47,596
I wonder how people back then
managed to get through it.

462
00:27:47,816 --> 00:27:49,676
I guess there were
many things involved.

463
00:27:50,546 --> 00:27:53,186
In the past, living as a couple

464
00:27:53,316 --> 00:27:55,286
was probably more practical
than being single.

465
00:27:55,876 --> 00:27:56,906
And then there's the financial side.

466
00:27:57,776 --> 00:27:59,106
If you find a good partner,

467
00:27:59,646 --> 00:28:02,406
they can probably lead you
toward a better life, right?

468
00:28:02,736 --> 00:28:05,066
It's actually a lot like a blind box.

469
00:28:05,976 --> 00:28:08,486
We were just lucky enough
to pull each other.

470
00:28:09,056 --> 00:28:10,246
We're both secret characters, aren't we?

471
00:28:10,656 --> 00:28:11,266
Yeah.

472
00:28:12,666 --> 00:28:14,176
- This one's good. Have you tried it?
- Oh, yeah?

473
00:28:14,266 --> 00:28:15,316
Here, try this one.

474
00:28:16,226 --> 00:28:16,886
Is it good?

475
00:28:17,116 --> 00:28:17,986
Want some sticky rice?

476
00:28:22,056 --> 00:28:24,406
Hi, Mom. What are you up to?

477
00:28:24,546 --> 00:28:26,136
(I'm just folding laundry.)

478
00:28:26,216 --> 00:28:28,926
Hey, let me send you something.
Hold on a sec.

479
00:28:28,956 --> 00:28:31,026
(Hmm? What are you sending me?)

480
00:28:31,326 --> 00:28:32,306
Just a second.

481
00:28:40,966 --> 00:28:41,966
Whoa.

482
00:28:44,456 --> 00:28:47,126
How does Dad look so young?

483
00:28:47,416 --> 00:28:48,646
It's an edited photo.

484
00:28:48,906 --> 00:28:50,976
He passed away so young.

485
00:28:51,096 --> 00:28:52,736
That's why he looks so young
in the photo.

486
00:28:52,806 --> 00:28:55,406
Is technology really
this advanced these days?

487
00:28:55,646 --> 00:28:58,566
Whoa, you picked out quite a big house.

488
00:29:02,126 --> 00:29:04,476
It would be great
if we could live in Phayao together.

489
00:29:09,866 --> 00:29:12,736
Mungkorn, you're just a subordinate.

490
00:29:13,046 --> 00:29:15,316
You have to stay
wherever they tell you to.

491
00:29:15,616 --> 00:29:17,566
(Just do what you can, okay?)

492
00:29:19,096 --> 00:29:21,236
Can't I at least dream?

493
00:29:22,626 --> 00:29:26,076
But dreams need a little luck
to go with them, sweetie.

494
00:29:28,696 --> 00:29:29,946
Mom, what's wrong?

495
00:29:30,096 --> 00:29:31,636
I'm fine, sweetie.

496
00:29:31,656 --> 00:29:32,916
I'm just coughing.

497
00:29:33,056 --> 00:29:35,186
(The weather's starting to get chilly.)

498
00:29:35,226 --> 00:29:37,526
(I'll head to bed in a bit.)

499
00:29:37,956 --> 00:29:39,166
(Talk to you later, okay?)

500
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:40,986
(I miss you, sweetie.)

501
00:29:41,016 --> 00:29:42,246
Make sure to take your medicine.

502
00:29:42,526 --> 00:29:43,536
Talk to you later.

503
00:29:43,826 --> 00:29:46,146
Okay. God bless you.

504
00:30:05,876 --> 00:30:08,336
(Mr. Mungkorn Phianwanich,
born on Monday, October 13, 1997)

505
00:30:11,326 --> 00:30:13,826
(Is there anything you want?
Just name it, and it's yours.)

506
00:30:14,326 --> 00:30:16,786
(The necklace from Titanic?
I'll go dive for it myself.)

507
00:30:37,116 --> 00:30:37,846
Whoa!

508
00:30:38,986 --> 00:30:40,976
Cupid, what are you doing here?

509
00:30:41,026 --> 00:30:43,446
I'm not Cupid. Call me Somrak.

510
00:30:43,476 --> 00:30:45,306
And who the hell is this?

511
00:30:45,566 --> 00:30:46,726
And this is Bee.

512
00:30:47,236 --> 00:30:49,336
- We're both ready to look after you
- We're both ready to look after you

513
00:30:49,336 --> 00:30:50,796
- twenty-four hours a day.
- twenty-four hours a day.

514
00:30:50,796 --> 00:30:52,826
Ugh, no way!

515
00:30:52,896 --> 00:30:54,266
You don't have a choice.

516
00:30:56,426 --> 00:30:58,726
For your safety, you need bodyguards.

517
00:30:58,986 --> 00:31:00,266
I insist.

518
00:31:02,666 --> 00:31:03,436
Why?

519
00:31:30,816 --> 00:31:32,326
You're supposed to do it on this side.

520
00:31:34,706 --> 00:31:35,516
Sh*t...

521
00:31:36,416 --> 00:31:37,276
Hey, stop right there!

522
00:31:37,296 --> 00:31:38,936
- Inspector, quick!
- I'm coming!

523
00:31:39,096 --> 00:31:41,146
- Stop, Mr. Thear.
- Wait!

524
00:31:41,166 --> 00:31:43,256
- It's dangerous!
- Mr. Thear, don't go.

525
00:31:43,286 --> 00:31:45,266
- Mr. Thear, it's dangerous!
- Inspector...

526
00:31:45,286 --> 00:31:46,896
- Follow me!
- Hold on. Don't go.

527
00:31:46,916 --> 00:31:48,966
- If Lady Pharada finds out, I'm dead.
- Please don't go.

528
00:31:48,986 --> 00:31:50,676
- Don't go. It's dangerous.
- It's too dangerous!

529
00:31:53,406 --> 00:31:54,706
What the hell is this?

530
00:32:03,636 --> 00:32:04,516
Inspector Thear,

531
00:32:04,736 --> 00:32:07,226
are those two being newly assigned here?

532
00:32:07,376 --> 00:32:09,566
I've seen them
hanging around the station all day.

533
00:32:10,276 --> 00:32:12,386
My mother sent them, sir.

534
00:32:12,416 --> 00:32:16,086
She's been very stressed
and paranoid lately,

535
00:32:16,926 --> 00:32:18,306
so she insisted on
having people protect me.

536
00:32:18,356 --> 00:32:21,846
Whatever you do,
make sure it's appropriate.

537
00:32:21,916 --> 00:32:24,366
We're police officers.
We're supposed to serve the people,

538
00:32:24,426 --> 00:32:26,966
not have the people taking care of us.

539
00:32:27,786 --> 00:32:29,306
It's ruining our professional image.

540
00:32:29,366 --> 00:32:30,286
Yes, sir.

541
00:32:30,606 --> 00:32:33,746
I'll deal with this immediately.

542
00:32:34,426 --> 00:32:35,166
Good.

543
00:32:39,266 --> 00:32:42,346
(Police Major Theartha Phiromsamorn,
Investigative Inspector)

544
00:32:51,136 --> 00:32:52,206
I'm done with this.

545
00:32:53,516 --> 00:32:55,346
How am I supposed to work

546
00:32:55,366 --> 00:32:56,746
if someone's
following me around all day?

547
00:32:56,916 --> 00:32:59,606
But nothing bad happened today, right?

548
00:32:59,846 --> 00:33:02,106
See? This works best.

549
00:33:02,206 --> 00:33:03,256
I'm a police officer.

550
00:33:03,556 --> 00:33:05,946
I can't have someone
watching over me day and night.

551
00:33:05,966 --> 00:33:07,636
What are the locals
going to think of me?

552
00:33:07,836 --> 00:33:09,806
Why don't you understand me at all?

553
00:33:10,346 --> 00:33:11,936
Then what do you want me to do?

554
00:33:12,146 --> 00:33:13,406
You won't get married.

555
00:33:13,696 --> 00:33:15,206
You won't let anyone protect you.

556
00:33:16,466 --> 00:33:18,576
If I could die in your place,
I would have done it already.

557
00:33:19,196 --> 00:33:19,906
Mom...

558
00:33:20,206 --> 00:33:21,606
Can you please try to understand me?

559
00:33:21,746 --> 00:33:24,066
I want to attend your wedding,
not your funeral.

560
00:33:28,536 --> 00:33:31,096
Oh, dear.

561
00:33:31,776 --> 00:33:33,026
My Lady...

562
00:33:34,366 --> 00:33:36,426
You have only one son,

563
00:33:36,686 --> 00:33:39,126
and he's both stubborn and mischievous.

564
00:33:39,276 --> 00:33:41,926
He never sees his mother's great love.

565
00:33:45,826 --> 00:33:51,226
♪Think of all the love a mother gave,♪

566
00:33:51,896 --> 00:33:55,056
- ♪What could ever be enough♪
- ♪What could ever be enough♪

567
00:33:55,196 --> 00:33:59,266
- ♪To match what she gave?♪
- ♪To match what she gave?♪

568
00:34:00,086 --> 00:34:02,436
- ♪Oh...♪
- It's only for six months, son.

569
00:34:05,406 --> 00:34:06,886
Just six short months.

570
00:34:08,456 --> 00:34:12,546
Could you please reconsider
just one more time?

571
00:34:33,676 --> 00:34:36,456
(Chiang Rai)

572
00:34:36,906 --> 00:34:38,116
Oh, Lieutenant Prang,

573
00:34:38,196 --> 00:34:40,546
please take these documents
downstairs for me.

574
00:34:45,676 --> 00:34:47,006
What should we have for dinner?

575
00:34:47,216 --> 00:34:48,286
How about some noodles?

576
00:34:49,606 --> 00:34:50,616
No, I'm bored of that.

577
00:34:50,886 --> 00:34:52,766
What do you want, then?

578
00:34:53,576 --> 00:34:54,739
It's up to you.

579
00:34:54,866 --> 00:34:55,799
Up to me?

580
00:34:56,726 --> 00:34:59,526
Then, can I eat you instead?

581
00:34:59,576 --> 00:35:01,446
I want you all day long. Can I eat you?

582
00:35:01,466 --> 00:35:03,326
- I don't know.
- You don't?

583
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:05,856
Come here.

584
00:35:06,865 --> 00:35:08,096
You're so adorable.

585
00:35:08,296 --> 00:35:11,586
Hey! This is a government building.
What do you think you're doing?

586
00:35:11,666 --> 00:35:12,546
I'll arrest you both.

587
00:35:14,716 --> 00:35:15,486
Good afternoon.

588
00:35:15,796 --> 00:35:19,166
How can I find a love like this, buddy?

589
00:35:19,426 --> 00:35:20,286
You want the truth?

590
00:35:20,476 --> 00:35:23,336
Someone like you
isn't likely to ever settle down.

591
00:35:25,376 --> 00:35:26,516
Still a smart-ass as always.

592
00:35:26,696 --> 00:35:28,746
Anyway, what brings you
all the way to Mae Sai?

593
00:35:28,996 --> 00:35:31,046
Wait, did you miss me?

594
00:35:31,386 --> 00:35:32,286
Not you,

595
00:35:32,696 --> 00:35:33,946
but Sergeant Mungkorn.

596
00:35:49,026 --> 00:35:50,306
Please marry me.

597
00:35:52,016 --> 00:35:52,926
Inspector Thear?

598
00:36:03,916 --> 00:36:05,386
I've been thinking it over.

599
00:36:06,406 --> 00:36:08,836
If I have to have bodyguards
tailing me for six months,

600
00:36:08,856 --> 00:36:10,606
I'd rather just get married
and be done with it.

601
00:36:10,746 --> 00:36:11,746
It won't be a bother to anyone else.

602
00:36:11,876 --> 00:36:13,286
It will be a bother to me.

603
00:36:13,326 --> 00:36:14,086
Why?

604
00:36:14,636 --> 00:36:16,826
Is it because you're dating someone?

605
00:36:17,266 --> 00:36:19,206
Well, no.

606
00:36:20,516 --> 00:36:22,506
You're my boss,
and I'm just your subordinate.

607
00:36:22,616 --> 00:36:24,016
Hey, how is that a problem?

608
00:36:24,046 --> 00:36:25,206
It's perfectly fine.

609
00:36:25,226 --> 00:36:26,996
I might not be as popular as you are,

610
00:36:27,936 --> 00:36:30,406
but I still cherish my freedom.

611
00:36:30,796 --> 00:36:34,246
Marrying me is a bigger deal
than getting a promotion.

612
00:36:34,346 --> 00:36:37,776
Anyone would jump at the chance
to take my last name.

613
00:36:37,806 --> 00:36:38,946
Well, count me out.

614
00:36:40,036 --> 00:36:41,086
Excuse me.

615
00:36:41,856 --> 00:36:42,666
Hey, wait!

616
00:36:44,526 --> 00:36:46,966
Please help me. I'm begging you.

617
00:36:46,986 --> 00:36:49,026
I'll give you anything you want.

618
00:36:49,876 --> 00:36:50,676
What do you want?

619
00:36:50,706 --> 00:36:53,126
Do you want me to get down on one knee
and propose?

620
00:36:53,246 --> 00:36:54,426
Fine, I'll do it right now.

621
00:36:54,446 --> 00:36:55,596
What are you doing, Inspector?

622
00:36:55,686 --> 00:36:56,236
Hey!

623
00:36:57,956 --> 00:36:59,006
Sergeant Mungkorn,

624
00:37:00,706 --> 00:37:02,496
will you marry me?

625
00:37:07,336 --> 00:37:10,156
I, Inspector Thear, solemnly swear...

626
00:37:11,286 --> 00:37:14,786
that I will be
a good husband to you forever.

627
00:37:39,666 --> 00:37:40,836
No way, Inspector.

628
00:37:41,026 --> 00:37:43,346
Come on, I'm begging you.

629
00:37:43,596 --> 00:37:46,386
Please help this handsome
but cursed Inspector.

630
00:37:46,576 --> 00:37:47,596
Please?

631
00:37:47,626 --> 00:37:49,846
What is it with you?
This is a huge deal for me.

632
00:37:50,586 --> 00:37:52,586
If anyone finds out, my life is ruined.

633
00:37:53,666 --> 00:37:55,536
Don't worry. No one will ever find out,

634
00:37:55,556 --> 00:37:56,976
except for our families.

635
00:37:59,086 --> 00:38:01,566
Please help me out.

636
00:38:02,166 --> 00:38:03,566
Inspector, stand up.

637
00:38:04,286 --> 00:38:05,446
Please, just get up.

638
00:38:13,206 --> 00:38:14,266
If you want me to marry you,

639
00:38:15,166 --> 00:38:16,506
I have three conditions.

640
00:38:16,626 --> 00:38:17,286
Name them.

641
00:38:18,246 --> 00:38:18,966
First,

642
00:38:20,316 --> 00:38:22,436
you have to give me one million baht.

643
00:38:22,846 --> 00:38:24,926
Whoa, one million?

644
00:38:25,276 --> 00:38:26,686
Wow, you're really
making the most of this.

645
00:38:28,266 --> 00:38:29,986
I'm gonna use it
to have a house built for my mom.

646
00:38:32,656 --> 00:38:34,096
A good son. I like that.

647
00:38:34,316 --> 00:38:35,206
Second,

648
00:38:36,186 --> 00:38:37,666
once we move to Chiang Mai,

649
00:38:38,036 --> 00:38:40,146
you have to let me
handle the major cases.

650
00:38:40,226 --> 00:38:42,666
You're this soft.
Can you really handle it?

651
00:38:42,926 --> 00:38:43,776
Third,

652
00:38:44,406 --> 00:38:45,966
after we get divorced,

653
00:38:47,476 --> 00:38:48,617
you have to tell your father

654
00:38:48,646 --> 00:38:49,906
to transfer me
to Mueang Phayao Police Station.

655
00:38:49,906 --> 00:38:50,766
Is that a deal?

656
00:39:03,076 --> 00:39:04,876
Otherwise, you can take your ring back.

657
00:39:06,276 --> 00:39:07,636
I'm not the one in trouble anyway.

658
00:39:07,656 --> 00:39:09,086
Whoa, whoa, hey!

659
00:39:10,676 --> 00:39:11,826
Calm down.

660
00:39:13,426 --> 00:39:14,636
As soon as the curse is gone,

661
00:39:15,126 --> 00:39:16,076
we divorce immediately.

662
00:39:16,136 --> 00:39:16,856
Deal.

663
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,076
(Marriage Certificate)

664
00:39:27,796 --> 00:39:30,606
And just like that,
you're officially a married couple.

665
00:39:31,096 --> 00:39:33,006
So, we're all set now, right?

666
00:39:33,136 --> 00:39:34,466
Not yet, dear.

667
00:39:34,506 --> 00:39:35,996
It's just the paperwork done.

668
00:39:36,016 --> 00:39:38,446
We still need the wedding ceremony
and the soul-binding ritual.

669
00:39:38,506 --> 00:39:39,966
Is that really necessary, Mom?

670
00:39:40,166 --> 00:39:42,676
Heaven and earth already know,
and so does the government.

671
00:39:42,696 --> 00:39:43,946
No can do, son.

672
00:39:43,966 --> 00:39:46,826
You have to make it look like
you're really a couple.

673
00:39:58,076 --> 00:39:59,926
Alright, if you're ready,

674
00:39:59,946 --> 00:40:03,676
allow me to introduce the grooms.

675
00:40:39,396 --> 00:40:40,586
At this very moment,

676
00:40:41,196 --> 00:40:44,796
the sun is positioned directly
over this sacred ground.

677
00:40:45,086 --> 00:40:46,536
It's a sign of the auspicious hour

678
00:40:46,566 --> 00:40:49,666
for both grooms to exchange rings,

679
00:40:49,686 --> 00:40:54,486
recite your vows to each other,

680
00:40:55,046 --> 00:40:57,506
and promise to keep those vows
from this moment on.

681
00:41:04,446 --> 00:41:07,166
I promise...

682
00:41:07,636 --> 00:41:09,556
to be a loving...

683
00:41:10,796 --> 00:41:12,386
and faithful husband to Mungkorn.

684
00:41:22,976 --> 00:41:26,566
I promise to be a good husband

685
00:41:27,166 --> 00:41:28,926
to share in both joy and sorrow

686
00:41:29,576 --> 00:41:31,226
and never leave your side.

687
00:41:37,906 --> 00:41:38,926
Mungkorn,

688
00:41:39,386 --> 00:41:42,606
I'm so grateful
that you agreed to marry Thear.

689
00:41:43,276 --> 00:41:45,866
Even if you don't have feelings
for each other yet,

690
00:41:45,936 --> 00:41:48,886
I hope you'll grow to love one another

691
00:41:48,936 --> 00:41:51,906
and stay destined for each other
like this forever.

692
00:41:52,586 --> 00:41:54,286
Now that you're married,

693
00:41:54,986 --> 00:41:57,506
you'd better cut out the womanizing.

694
00:41:58,156 --> 00:42:01,296
Jeez, Dad. What kind of person
do you take me for?

695
00:42:01,476 --> 00:42:02,476
A decent person.

696
00:42:03,266 --> 00:42:03,956
Come on, honey.

697
00:42:04,176 --> 00:42:04,826
He is.

698
00:42:06,826 --> 00:42:09,506
Please take good care of Mungkorn,
Inspector Thear.

699
00:42:09,826 --> 00:42:12,456
Always talk things through
when you have problems.

700
00:42:12,946 --> 00:42:17,906
In a marriage, if one is fire,
the other must be water.

701
00:42:18,106 --> 00:42:19,236
Okay, Mom.

702
00:42:19,686 --> 00:42:21,626
I'm ready to be the fire...

703
00:42:22,286 --> 00:42:23,886
that burns Mungkorn up.

704
00:42:24,816 --> 00:42:26,556
And I'll be the water...

705
00:42:27,116 --> 00:42:28,736
to drown Inspector Thear in.

706
00:42:42,746 --> 00:42:44,236
Remember this.

707
00:42:45,416 --> 00:42:47,166
After the ceremony is over,

708
00:42:48,196 --> 00:42:54,706
you two must share a bed

709
00:42:55,196 --> 00:42:59,306
and become one
in the most intimate way.

710
00:43:15,256 --> 00:43:16,496
Otherwise,

711
00:43:17,426 --> 00:43:20,866
this soul-binding will not be complete,

712
00:43:21,766 --> 00:43:24,636
and fate will continue to haunt you.

713
00:43:25,636 --> 00:43:29,506
You two must love each other
as much as you possibly can

714
00:43:29,716 --> 00:43:34,606
for the heavens and earth
are watching you.

715
00:43:41,446 --> 00:43:42,646
Next,

716
00:43:44,016 --> 00:43:45,796
give each other a tender kiss

717
00:43:46,456 --> 00:43:49,466
to seal your love.

718
00:43:51,086 --> 00:43:52,926
Kiss... now.

719
00:43:52,946 --> 00:43:56,466
Kiss! Kiss!

720
00:43:56,696 --> 00:43:59,736
- Just kiss him, son.
- Kiss! Kiss!

721
00:43:59,879 --> 00:44:01,232
You're good at it, aren't you?

722
00:44:01,386 --> 00:44:03,566
Kiss! Kiss!

723
00:44:03,586 --> 00:44:04,506
Kiss him already.

724
00:44:29,736 --> 00:44:31,086
For the next part of the ceremony,

725
00:44:31,116 --> 00:44:34,966
we ask the parents of the grooms

726
00:44:35,006 --> 00:44:38,146
to escort the newlyweds
to their wedding chamber.

727
00:44:38,666 --> 00:44:40,096
We have to go to
the wedding chamber together?

728
00:44:40,206 --> 00:44:42,046
Well, of course, Mr. Mungkorn!

729
00:44:42,546 --> 00:44:47,246
Tonight, you have to sleep
in Mr. Thear's room.

730
00:44:48,376 --> 00:44:53,226
Most importantly,
you must stay together all night.

731
00:44:54,466 --> 00:44:57,146
You are strictly forbidden
from leaving the room.

732
00:45:20,516 --> 00:45:21,966
Is the closet space enough for you?

733
00:45:22,156 --> 00:45:23,726
If it's not, just let me know.

734
00:45:25,296 --> 00:45:27,086
It's not like I'm moving in permanently.

735
00:45:27,476 --> 00:45:28,826
This is more than enough.

736
00:45:29,856 --> 00:45:31,686
And why are you wearing those pajamas?

737
00:45:32,026 --> 00:45:33,206
They look so worn out.

738
00:45:33,536 --> 00:45:34,516
Do you want to wear some of mine?

739
00:45:34,536 --> 00:45:35,496
No, thanks.

740
00:45:36,376 --> 00:45:37,786
I'm used to these.

741
00:45:44,066 --> 00:45:46,936
But don't worry.
They're definitely clean.

742
00:45:53,326 --> 00:45:55,846
If you're done, please go get dressed

743
00:45:56,976 --> 00:45:58,376
so I can set up the bed.

744
00:45:58,646 --> 00:46:00,096
Go ahead, then.

745
00:46:00,646 --> 00:46:01,516
Why?

746
00:46:02,036 --> 00:46:02,906
Are you blushing?

747
00:46:03,006 --> 00:46:05,516
Don't be ridiculous.
I've got it, too. Why would I?

748
00:46:05,546 --> 00:46:07,696
Exactly, why would you?

749
00:46:07,996 --> 00:46:09,906
I'll just make myself comfortable, then.

750
00:46:09,926 --> 00:46:12,706
Might as well strip down completely.

751
00:46:16,886 --> 00:46:19,886
Hey, I'm your husband now.

752
00:46:20,476 --> 00:46:23,176
Seeing a bit of each other is fine.
I don't mind.

753
00:46:23,826 --> 00:46:25,036
Well, I do.

754
00:46:28,686 --> 00:46:30,686
Don't forget, Inspector,

755
00:46:31,256 --> 00:46:33,876
that you're just a counterfeit husband.

756
00:46:35,116 --> 00:46:35,886
It's fake, you know.

757
00:46:35,906 --> 00:46:39,606
Please, it's not like
I'm actually attracted to you.

758
00:46:39,666 --> 00:46:42,036
Once this marriage
to fix my luck is over,

759
00:46:42,066 --> 00:46:46,046
I'll have to mend the hearts
of all the girls lining up for me.

760
00:46:46,126 --> 00:46:49,016
Man, the line is never-ending.

761
00:46:49,036 --> 00:46:51,046
It's longer
than the stairway to Doi Suthep.

762
00:46:51,166 --> 00:46:52,286
Whatever you say.

763
00:46:52,536 --> 00:46:55,306
And if it really is that long,

764
00:46:56,466 --> 00:46:59,946
then I wish them a blessed pilgrimage.

765
00:47:12,626 --> 00:47:13,976
Why are you sleeping over there?

766
00:47:14,456 --> 00:47:15,746
Come here and sleep on the bed.

767
00:47:17,406 --> 00:47:19,046
I prefer sleeping by myself.

768
00:47:19,766 --> 00:47:21,106
I don't like sharing a bed with anyone.

769
00:47:23,926 --> 00:47:25,276
What do you mean "anyone"?

770
00:47:25,766 --> 00:47:26,856
It's just me.

771
00:47:27,336 --> 00:47:28,936
We've known each other for ages.

772
00:47:29,583 --> 00:47:31,639
The more I know you,
the less I want to share a bed with you.

773
00:47:35,466 --> 00:47:37,479
Inspector, that hurts!

774
00:47:41,126 --> 00:47:42,526
Stop calling me "Inspector."

775
00:47:43,106 --> 00:47:44,726
Why don't you try calling me...

776
00:47:45,126 --> 00:47:48,026
husband?

777
00:47:51,086 --> 00:47:53,166
Alright, Husband.

778
00:47:53,866 --> 00:47:54,746
Can we go to sleep now?

779
00:48:07,916 --> 00:48:10,916
If you want to come up here,
I don't mind.

780
00:48:14,476 --> 00:48:16,366
You could even sneak a hug.

781
00:48:16,836 --> 00:48:18,426
I'm always ready to do that.

782
00:48:25,816 --> 00:48:26,746
I'm not buying that.

783
00:48:28,250 --> 00:48:30,123
♪Trying...♪

784
00:48:37,396 --> 00:48:40,686
Good night, "Husband."

785
00:48:44,356 --> 00:48:46,016
Am I doing the right thing here?

786
00:48:47,851 --> 00:48:52,711
♪I'm just a name on your contract,
you're just passing through,♪

787
00:48:52,736 --> 00:48:57,536
♪So stay on your side,
and I'll stay on mine, too♪

788
00:48:57,556 --> 00:49:02,466
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

789
00:49:02,496 --> 00:49:07,326
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

790
00:49:07,356 --> 00:49:11,626
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

791
00:49:11,656 --> 00:49:17,122
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

792
00:49:17,356 --> 00:49:20,826
♪It's time you became mine♪

793
00:49:21,203 --> 00:49:22,643
What are you doing in here?

794
00:49:22,668 --> 00:49:24,449
Afraid I'll see your willy?

795
00:49:24,474 --> 00:49:25,983
I've never been with anyone like this.

796
00:49:26,008 --> 00:49:27,343
You'd better get used to it.

797
00:49:27,522 --> 00:49:28,409
I mean my body.

798
00:49:28,605 --> 00:49:30,405
Inspector, are you okay?

799
00:49:30,430 --> 00:49:31,392
Of course I am.

800
00:49:31,438 --> 00:49:34,038
We'll only act like lovey-dovey husbands

801
00:49:34,100 --> 00:49:34,906
at home.

802
00:49:35,073 --> 00:49:36,403
Once we're outside,

803
00:49:36,428 --> 00:49:38,206
we're just boss and subordinate.

804
00:49:38,240 --> 00:49:39,966
And don't tell anyone about this.

805
00:49:39,991 --> 00:49:40,953
I'm here to remind you
about the promise.

806
00:49:40,978 --> 00:49:42,341
You said once we got married,

807
00:49:42,365 --> 00:49:43,403
you'd let me handle the major cases.

808
00:49:43,428 --> 00:49:45,700
What if I break that promise?

809
00:49:45,810 --> 00:49:47,023
Will you tell everyone...

810
00:49:47,048 --> 00:49:48,268
Inspector Thear and I are...

811
00:49:52,343 --> 00:49:57,253
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

812
00:49:57,283 --> 00:50:02,113
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

813
00:50:02,143 --> 00:50:06,413
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

814
00:50:06,443 --> 00:50:11,969
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

815
00:50:11,994 --> 00:50:16,861
♪Let's call off the deal
and let our hearts decide♪

816
00:50:16,892 --> 00:50:23,325
♪From contracting parties to lovers,
does that sound alright?♪

817
00:50:29,576 --> 00:50:33,046
♪It's time you became mine♪
